{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791305780,"nonce":"HBJW05IixDog3jy4hKynEmNCspQ=","title":"Normalize runtime integer predicates to Haxe booleans","message":"A native predicate with an i32 return was retained as an i32 register even when the Haxe expression type was Bool. Unary ! consequently emitted integer bitwise not: a successful EReg.match produced 1, then ! produced -2 and entered the failure branch. Native Haxe passes RuntimeBooleanResults.hx; the prior compiler throws negated match.\n\nmaybe_unbox_for_extern_return now compares integer returns against zero when the declared result is Bool. The native function keeps its actual signature; Haxe consumers receive a Bool register. RuntimeBooleanResults covers negation, double negation, passing a predicate result as a Bool argument, Boolean array storage, string predicates, and filesystem predicates. The regression passes native Haxe, tiered execution, and pinned Cranelift. ERegConstructor also passes after normalization.\n\nAll 115 regressions pass. Workspace fmt and Clippy across all features and targets with -D warnings pass. Full conformance comparison is running against the 858/1094 macro-captures baseline.","files":null}]}